{
  "raw": {
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/AMER2025": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Department of American Culture and Literature",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Department of American Culture and Literature | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in Department of American Culture and Literature × Applications for this position has been closed. The Department of American Culture and Literature at Bilkent University invites applications for two positions at the assistant professor level to begin in September 2026. Those with primary fields in American studies, history, literature, film and media, theater, gender studies, critical race and ethnic studies are invited to apply. Candidates should hold a PhD at the time of appointment. Applicants should be able to teach one or more of our first- and second-year courses—Introduction to American Studies, Methods and Texts, Texts and Contexts, and Introduction to American History—as well as courses pertinent to the applicant’s specialty within the range of our third- and fourth-year courses. As research is a priority at Bilkent University, its support includes grants for conference travel and the possibility of sabbatical leave following the third year. Bilkent University , located in suburban Ankara, is a non-profit foundation university supported by its own endowment. It is home to a vibrant international community, with faculty members from 40 different countries. The language of instruction across the university is English. The university offers a generous benefits package including on-campus housing, health insurance, and subsidized private school for faculty members' dependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. Applicants must upload a (i) cover letter (ii) CV (iii) research statement (iv) teaching statement, and (v) writing sample. In addition, (vi) candidates are required to provide contact details for at least three referees. All applications submitted before November 10, 2025 will receive full consideration. For further information on the position, please contact Daniel Johnson, Chair, Department of American Culture and Literature, at: daniel.johnson@bilkent.edu.tr . Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/HART2026": {
      "title": "One position (rank: Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor),",
      "description": "One position (rank: Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor), at the Department of Archaeology, commencing September 2026 | Applications for Faculty Positions One position (rank: Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor), at the Department of Archaeology, commencing September 2026 × Applications for this position has been closed. The Department of Archaeology at Bilkent University invites applications for one full-time faculty position at the level of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor. This position is part of our broader initiative to build capacity for interdisciplinary research and teaching within one of Türkiye’s leading archaeology departments. We are seeking researchers with a dynamic, interdisciplinary background and strong research ties to Anatolia or surrounding regions. Although research area is open, we especially welcome applications from scholars specializing in Classical Archaeology, Archaeological Science and/or Digital Archaeology. Minimum requirements are a PhD in Archaeology at the time of the appointment, a clearly defined research agenda, and publications in internationally noted journals or presses. Candidates should be able to teach specialized topics in their research field at the graduate level, as well as general courses in Archaeology at the undergraduate level. The Department of Archaeology is an expanding institution that currently offers an undergraduate program and a Master’s program; a PhD program is planned for the near future. The Department’s programs focus on the Neolithic, Bronze and Iron Ages as well as the Greek, Roman and Medieval archaeology of Anatolia and surrounding regions. Our team of specialists, who are all active researchers, help students explore the material remains of the many peoples that have populated and passed through this dynamic geography. We place importance on hands-on experience for students both in our departmental laboratories and through an internship program at sites across the country. The Department is directly affiliated with a number of outstanding archaeological sites in Anatolia, including Aphrodisias, Sagalassos and Türkmen-Karahöyük. Further information about the Department can be found on the department website: http://arkeo.bilkent.edu.tr Bilkent University, located in Ankara, is a non-profit foundation university supported by its own endowment. It is home to a vibrant international community. Its faculty members come from 40 different countries, and the language of instruction across the university is English. Bilkent University is committed to a diverse and inclusive workplace. It is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, national origin, gender, disability, or age. The university offers a generous benefits package including on-campus housing, health insurance, and subsidized private school for faculty members' dependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. As research is a priority at Bilkent University, its support includes grants for conference travel and the possibility of sabbatical leave following the third year of employment. Informal inquiries are welcome and should be addressed to Peter Talloen ( peter.talloen@bilkent.edu.tr ). Applicants will need to apply online using the university’s online application system: https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/HART2026 Applications will be accepted until January 16, 2026, 23:59:59 local time (GMT + 3) They must upload a (i) cover letter, (ii) CV, (iii) research statement (max. 500 words), (iv) teaching statement (max. 500 words), and (v) representative sample of the candidate's publications. In addition, (vi) candidates are required to provide contact details for at least three referees. The initial interview will be held online and letters of recommendation will be requested for short-listed candidates. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/ARCH2026": {
      "title": "Open Rank Assistant / Associate / Full Professor of Architecture in Building Science",
      "description": "Open Rank Assistant / Associate / Full Professor of Architecture in Building Science | Applications for Faculty Positions Open Rank Assistant / Associate / Full Professor of Architecture in Building Science × Applications for this position has been closed. Open Rank Assistant / Associate / Full Professor of Architecture in Building Science Bilkent University Department of Architecture Ankara, Turkey Type: Full-Time (12 Months) Salary: Commensurate with experience Post Date: October 10, 2025 Start Date: September 1, 2026 Category: Architecture Position Description: The Department of Architecture at Bilkent University invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position in Architecture, with a preferred research and teaching focus on building science, structural systems, sustainability, acoustics, and building materials. Applicants should demonstrate an active record of research and publication, as well as a clear commitment to developing a strong scholarly agenda. The expected teaching load is 3–3, typically consisting of one design studio (counting as two courses) and one lecture/seminar course each semester. Responsibilities also include advising undergraduate (B.Arch) and graduate (M.Sc.) students, as well as contributing to the intellectual life of the department through core courses, electives, and graduate seminars. The anticipated start date of the position is September 1, 2026. Candidates should hold a Ph.D. in building science or a closely related discipline by the start date of the appointment; applicants who are ABD will be considered, provided that the degree is completed before September 1, 2026. The successful candidate will demonstrate evidence of a substantial and sustainable research program, a strong record of publication, and a clear commitment to excellence in teaching and advising. Experience with undergraduate and graduate education, including design studios, lecture courses, and seminars, is highly desirable. Equally important is a demonstrated ability to work collegially and effectively with students and colleagues from diverse backgrounds. The department particularly values candidates who show a commitment to advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion through their teaching, research, and service. Applicants are encouraged to highlight inclusive practices in curriculum development, pedagogy, mentoring, and departmental culture in their cover letters. This is a 12-month tenure-track or tenured appointment with full university benefits (including healthcare, retirement plan, research support, and housing assistance). Applicants should submit the following materials: A cover letter describing qualifications for the position, as well as current and future research plans. A teaching statement. A current curriculum vitae. A representative sample of scholarly work (published or unpublished, not to exceed 30 pages). Contact information (mail, email, and phone) for three academic references. (Optional) Evidence of teaching excellence (e.g., teaching evaluations). Applications received by 10th of January 2026 will receive full consideration, but the position will remain open until filled. Materials should be uploaded to https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/ARCH2026 . Inquiries may be directed to the Search Committee Chair Bülent Batuman, batuman@bilkent.edu.tr . Bilkent University Founded in 1984 as Turkey’s first non-profit private university, Bilkent University brings together a vibrant international community of scholars and students. “Bilkent,” an acronym for Bilim Kenti (City of Science and Knowledge), is home to nine faculties, five schools, 30 undergraduate majors, and 59 graduate programs. The University Library is one of the most comprehensive in the region, housing nearly 3 million items and providing access to more than 250 databases, with over 600,000 annual visitors. Bilkent’s faculty members represent over 37 countries, while students come from more than 60. Located in western Ankara, the university’s three campuses form an academic hub in the city’s green western corridor. Bilkent is also part of a wider network of 19 universities in Ankara, including nine schools of architecture. For more information, please visit: https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent/ Department of Architecture The Department of Architecture at Bilkent University offers an interdisciplinary curriculum that bridges the humanities, computational sciences, building sciences, and design. This foundation is reinforced by professional training, including internships and practical experience. Our framework encourages students to develop critical and adaptive approaches to architecture, preparing them to engage with complex spatial, cultural, and technological challenges in a global context. Alongside teaching, the department fosters a dynamic research culture. Faculty and students contribute to fields such as design methods, history and theory, sustainability, heritage, and building technologies. As a young department, Bilkent Architecture has quickly established itself with a strong record of internationally competitive graduates, many of whom continue their studies at leading institutions worldwide or enter professional practice in architecture and allied fields. For more information, please visit: arch.bilkent.edu.tr Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/ELED2024": {
      "title": "Open Rank Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Elementary Teacher Education",
      "description": "Open Rank Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Elementary Teacher Education | Applications for Faculty Positions Open Rank Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Elementary Teacher Education Open Rank Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Elementary Teacher Education Position: Multiple full-time tenure-track positions in Elementary Teacher Education Bilkent University, Department of Elementary Education, Ankara, Turkey, invites applications for multiple full-time tenure-track faculty positions in Elementary Teacher Education. We are offering an innovative curriculum, seeking passionate educators with a strong commitment to developing highly skilled aspiring educators. Responsibilities include: Develop and deliver undergraduate and graduate courses in elementary education. Develop and maintain an active scholarly agenda. Disseminate research findings through peer-reviewed scholarly publications. Advise undergraduate and graduate students, including guiding graduate theses. Supervise pre-service teachers during their practicum experiences, and collaborate with mentor teachers in partner schools Foster a positive and collaborative learning environment for students, faculty and partner schools. Qualifications and Experience: A doctoral-level degree in Elementary Education, Curriculum and Instruction with a concentration in Elementary Education or a closely related field. Demonstrated potential for excellence in research, with a strong publication record and a clear research agenda. Relevant teaching experience in higher education. Experience in supervising pre-service teachers is highly desirable. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. To Apply: Submit a letter of interest, CV, research statement and teaching statement along with contact information for five academic referees. Salary and Benefits: We offer a competitive salary package commensurate with qualifications and experience. Additionally, benefits include rent-free furnished on campus housing, air-fare, paid annual leave, and comprehensive health coverage. Bilkent University is an equal opportunity employer. About Us: Bilkent University is an English medium private research university committed to fostering diversity and inclusion. Nestled in the heart of in Ankara, Turkey, the cradle of civilizations, Bilkent University stands as a beacon of academic excellence, with its diverse educational programs, scientific and scholarly research endeavors, and artistic and cultural activities. Our institution is dedicated to nurturing critical, analytical and independent thinkers, empowering individual as life-long learners. With a vibrant international community boasting over 700 faculty members from 34 countries, and a student body of approximately 13,000 students across 10 faculties, Bilkent University offers an unparalleled environment for intellectual growth and exploration. Our renowned Symphony Orchestra hosts around 30 concerts annually, featuring world-class performers, enriching our campus with artistic splendor and cultural vibrancy ( https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent/ ). Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/CHEM2025": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Department of Chemistry",
      "description": "Faculty Positions in Department of Chemistry | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Positions in Department of Chemistry The Department of Chemistry at Bilkent University seeks candidates for permanent and visiting faculty positions at all levels starting in February and September 2025. We seek persons with a Ph.D. in Chemistry or related fields. Faculty duties include teaching at the graduate and undergraduate levels, research, and supervision of student research. Specific examples of research programs of interest include materials science, biochemistry and polymer chemistry. The successful candidates will be expected to carry a vigorous research program and attract external research funding. Considerable central resources are available at Bilkent that can strengthen the research program and support interdisciplinary and collaborative research efforts. Salary is competitive and on-campus housing is provided to successful applicants.  Almost all students have tuition waivers and faculty member salary is guaranteed for 12 months. Bilkent University boasts a beautiful campus, conveniently located about 8 km from the city center of Ankara, in a serene and pleasant neighborhood. Applications consisting of a cover letter, a resume, a statement of teaching philosophy,  statement of research interests, and the names and addresses of at least two references, should be submitted electronically to the Search Committee: https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/CHEM2025. Applications will be reviewed as they are received on an ongoing basis and the search will continue until the positions are filled. For assistance, contact Associate Professor Burak Ülgüt, Chair, burakulgut@bilkent.edu.tr Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/COMD2026RF": {
      "title": "Open rank position for Research Faculty in the Department of Communication and Design",
      "description": "Open rank position for Research Faculty in the Department of Communication and Design | Applications for Faculty Positions Open rank position for Research Faculty in the Department of Communication and Design The Department of Communication and Design at Bilkent University invites applicants to join our research faculty beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year. The department welcomes applications from scholars working in any area of specialization within the field of media and communication studies. The position is open rank for assistant professors or higher. The language of instruction at Bilkent University is English. Successful candidates will have a strong existing publication record and be expected to continue producing peer-reviewed, internationally published research throughout their appointment. They will also contribute to the in-class teaching of both undergraduate and graduate courses, as well as supervise B.A. capstone projects and M.A. theses for our program in Media and Visual Studies. The expected teaching load is three courses per semester, with the possibility of a reduction for the first 2-4 semesters. The appointment also requires service to the University and the field. Research faculty application requirements: Ph.D. in media studies, communications, or a closely related subject. Degree MUST be in hand before the contract period begins. Demonstrated record of research success, including publication in refereed, international journal(s). Teaching experience Experience with media production preferred, but not required Candidates are expected to teach a range of media studies courses from the core department curriculum, plus advanced lecture courses and graduate seminars in their area of research. They are also expected to advise undergraduates and graduate students enrolled in our M.A. program in Media and Visual Studies. Target fields for the research faculty position include: Media industries Transnational screen studies, especially television Documentary Digital cultures Gaming and immersive media Organizational/strategic communication Risk, science, crisis, environmental communication Audience and reception studies As the first English-medium, not-for-profit private research university in Türkiye, world rankings regularly highlight Bilkent’s place as one of the leading global universities. The faculty at Bilkent University is comprised of academic staff from around 40 different countries. The university offers its research faculty on-campus housing in Ankara, discounted private school tuition (PK-12, IB curriculum) for dependents, subsidized childcare for preschool-aged children, lunch vouchers, access to private health care, and a variety of facilities and opportunities for its staff. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. The Department of Communication and Design has approximately 300 undergraduate majors, 25 graduate students in the Media and Visual Studies M.A. program, and a thriving undergraduate minor program. In addition, COMD offers selected courses as university-wide electives that reflect the university's foundational objectives of providing high-quality education, producing high-impact research, and developing critical and analytical thinking. For more information about Bilkent University and the Department of Communication and Design, please visit w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent/ and www.comd.bilkent.edu.tr Applicants should submit: Cover letter detailing the applicant’s research agenda and teaching activities CV Writing sample(s) of approx. 20 pages in total (PDF) Contact information for three recommenders Additional materials may be requested at a later time. Applications will be reviewed as they are received. The position(s) will remain open to applications until filled. Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/COMD2026SPF": {
      "title": "Open rank position for Studio Production Faculty in the Department of Communication and Design",
      "description": "Open rank position for Studio Production Faculty in the Department of Communication and Design | Applications for Faculty Positions Open rank position for Studio Production Faculty in the Department of Communication and Design The Department of Communication and Design at Bilkent University invites applications to join our studio production faculty beginning the 2026-2027 academic year. The department welcomes scholar-practitioners with experience in audiovisual production and/or other closely related arts. The position is open rank for full-time instructors or above. The language of instruction at Bilkent University is English. Successful candidates will have a strong record of accomplishment in the field and be expected to continue producing media and/or audiovisual work throughout their appointment. They will also contribute to the in-class teaching of undergraduates, particularly studio courses, as well as supervise B.A. capstone projects. The expected teaching load is four courses per semester, and the appointment also requires service to the University and the field. Studio faculty application requirements: MA/MFA/PhD in a related subject Professional experience in the designated field Prior classroom teaching experience Candidates are expected to teach a range of production courses from the core department curriculum, and advise undergraduate capstone projects. Target fields for the research faculty position include: Videography and digital filmmaking Fundamentals of audiovisual production Immersive media production Game design As the first English-medium, not-for-profit private research university in Türkiye, world rankings regularly highlight Bilkent’s place as one of the leading global universities. The faculty at Bilkent University comprises academic staff from around 40 countries. The university offers its faculty a robust benefits package, including discounted private school tuition (PK-12, IB curriculum) for dependents, subsidized childcare for preschool-aged children, lunch vouchers, access to private health care, and a variety of facilities and opportunities for its staff. The Department of Communication and Design has approximately 300 undergraduate majors, 25 graduate students in the Media and Visual Studies M.A. program, and a thriving undergraduate minor program. In addition, COMD offers selected courses as university-wide electives that reflect the university's foundational objectives of providing high-quality education, producing high-impact research, and developing critical and analytical thinking. For more information about Bilkent University and the Department of Communication and Design, please visit w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent/ and www.comd.bilkent.edu.tr Applicants should submit: Cover letter detailing the applicant’s production experience and teaching activities CV Portfolio of creative work (PDF with links or online portfolio; 3–5 representative works) Contact information for three recommenders, including at least one professional contact and at least one academic scholar. Additional materials may be requested at a later time. Applications will be reviewed as they are received. The position(s) will remain open to applications until filled. Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/CS2021": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Department of Computer Engineering to Start in 2026",
      "description": "Faculty Positions in Department of Computer Engineering to Start in 2026 | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Positions in Department of Computer Engineering to Start in 2026 The Computer Engineering Department at Bilkent University aims to hire multiple new faculty members to start in 2026 and seeks candidates for the positions. Appointments can be made at Assistant Professor, as well as at Associate Professor or Full Professor ranks for candidates with commensurate experiences and accomplishments. The department emphasizes both high quality research and teaching. Faculty duties include teaching at the graduate and undergraduate levels, research, supervision of theses and other related tasks. The department will consider candidates with backgrounds and interests in all areas of Computer Engineering and Science.  The department offers B.S,  M.S., and Ph.D. degrees, and its B.S. program is accredited by ABET. It is one of the top computer engineering departments in Turkey and attracts many of Turkey’s brightest high school graduates. Bilkent University is the first non-profit foundation university in Turkey. At Bilkent we place great emphasis on interdisciplinary research, university-industry collaboration, and innovative teaching. The university offers internationally competitive salaries and benefit packages including furnished housing on the University campus, health and retirement benefits as well as subsidized private school for faculty members' dependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. Bilkent University is recognized and ranked internationally as the premier institution of higher education in Turkey. It prides itself on its truly international perspective. The medium of instruction at Bilkent is English, and its international community of scholars and students coming from 40 different countries form an essential component of the university’s academic and social life. Ph.D. in computer science or a related discipline by the start of employment and evidence of exceptional research promise are required. Applications should be submitted online using the submit button below. Each application should describe the professional interests and goals of the candidate in both teaching and research, include a resume and the names and contact information of three or more individuals who will provide letters of recommendation. The evaluation of applications will start immediately and continue until positions are filled. More information about our department and programs is available at http://w3.cs.bilkent.edu.tr/ , and more information about Bilkent University is available at https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr . All questions regarding the available positions can be forwarded to the department chair through chair@cs.bilkent.edu.tr. Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/CTIS2024": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Department of Information Systems and Technologies",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Department of Information Systems and Technologies | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in Department of Information Systems and Technologies Department of Information Systems and Technologies of Faculty of Applied Sciences at Bilkent University invites applicants for the full-time Instructor position. Qualifications: Minimum M.Sc. degree (with Thesis) in Information Systems, Software Engineering, Computer Science/Engineering or related field. Work or teaching experience in one or more of the following areas: o.o. programming, software engineering, information systems, computer networks, computer/network security, or data analysis. Applicants who meet the above criteria should submit a letter of interest, an up-to-date CV, and two letters of recommendation through this system. Candidates are expected to actively engage in teaching and service to the department, faculty, and university. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the review will continue until the position will be filled. All questions regarding the available position(s) can be forwarded to the department chair through eucar@bilkent.edu.tr More information about our department and programs is available at http://www.ctis.bilkent.edu.tr and more information about Bilkent University is available at https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/EEE_Neuroscience_2015": {
      "title": "Electrical Engineering Faculty with Research Interest in Neuroscience",
      "description": "Electrical Engineering Faculty with Research Interest in Neuroscience | Applications for Faculty Positions Electrical Engineering Faculty with Research Interest in Neuroscience × Applications for this position has been closed. Bilkent University, Department of Electrical and Electronics Engineering The Department of Electrical and Electronics Engineering at Bilkent University seeks several highly qualified \napplicants for full-time faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor effective September 2017. Candidates are sought with a PhD degree in electrical and electronics engineering or a closely related \ndiscipline and a proven track record of research and strong commitment to teaching at undergraduate and \ngraduate levels. Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to, electronics, energy efficient \ncomputing/hardware systems, embedded systems, machine learning, computational neuroscience and electromagnetics. Bilkent University is a non-profit foundation university supported by its own endowment. Bilkent is a vibrant \ninternational community; faculty members come from 40 different countries, and the language of instruction across \nthe university is English. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. The university offers a \ngenerous benefit package including on-campus housing, health and retirement benefits as well as subsidized private \nschool for faculty members' dependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. The application folder must include a CV, Research Statement, Teaching Statement, and names of three references. \nApplications will be reviewed as they are received and the review will continue until the positions are filled. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/ELIT2026": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in the Department of English Language and Literature, Bilkent University",
      "description": "Faculty Position in the Department of English Language and Literature, Bilkent University | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in the Department of English Language and Literature, Bilkent University × Applications for this position has been closed. The Department of English Language and Literature at Bilkent University, Ankara, invites applications for a faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. Applications from scholars with research interests in any subfield of British or global Anglophone literatures are welcome. Minimum requirements are a Ph.D. in English or Comparative Literature in hand by May 2026, a good teaching record, and a clearly defined research agenda. Candidates should be able to offer specialized teaching in their research field, and should also be well prepared to teach across various genres and periods in English literature. The starting date for this post is September 2026. The Department of English Language and Literature currently offers an undergraduate program that covers British, Irish, and postcolonial literatures, and ranges from the medieval period to the present.  Further information about the department can be found on the department website: https://elit.bilkent.edu.tr . Bilkent University was founded in 1984 with the fundamental aim of creating a center of excellence in higher education and research; a non-profit foundation university supported by its own endowment, it is home to a vibrant international community. Faculty members come from 34 different countries, and the language of instruction across the university is English. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. The university offers a generous benefits package including on-campus housing and health and retirement benefits, as well as subsidized private school for faculty members' dependents. Inquiries about the position should be addressed to Ayşe Çelikkol ( celikkol@bilkent.edu.tr ) or Madeleine Read ( mread@bilkent.edu.tr ). Applications should include a cover letter, a CV, a short statement (maximum 500 words) of the applicant's teaching philosophy, a 1-2 page research statement, an article-length writing sample, and a list of three referees. Letters of recommendation will be requested for short-listed candidates. Applications received by December 19, 2025 will be given full consideration. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/MATEFL2021": {
      "title": "...",
      "description": "... | Applications for Faculty Positions ... × Applications for this position has been closed. Dear Prospective Applicants, Thank you for your interest in our department. We regret to inform you that there are no open positions available at present. However, we value your interest and encourage talented and qualified candidates to submit their applications to us for future reference. If you would like to apply, please send us a letter of interest, a detailed CV, a teaching statement, and a research statement, along with contact information for five academic referees. We kindly request that all application materials be submitted online . Sincerely, MA in TEFL Program Department of English Language Teaching Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/ESCI2021": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position, Curriculum & Instruction and Teacher Education, Department of Educational Sciences",
      "description": "Open Rank Faculty Position, Curriculum & Instruction and Teacher Education, Department of Educational Sciences | Applications for Faculty Positions Open Rank Faculty Position, Curriculum & Instruction and Teacher Education, Department of Educational Sciences × Applications for this position has been closed. Open Rank Faculty Position, Curriculum & Instruction, Department of Educational Sciences The Department of Educational Sciences at Bilkent University invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty position beginning September 2023. The candidate is expected to teach a range of courses in the MA and PhD programs in Curriculum and Instruction; have experience in teacher preparation and training, working with both pre-service and  in-service teachers demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching excellence, academic advising, thesis supervision, and academic service; demonstrate evidence of an active research agenda, and a record of publication in reputable journals Qualifications include a doctoral degree in Curriculum & Instruction, or a closely related area, and preferably a qualified teacher status. Graduate-level teaching experience which might include but not limited to the following areas will be an advantage: Philosophy of Education, Sociology of Education, Psychology of Education. To apply online : The application package should be submitted online , and it should include the following: a letter of interest, a detailed CV, a teaching statement, and a research statement along with contact information for five academic referees. About Bilkent University: Bilkent University was founded in 1984 with the fundamental aims of creating a center of excellence in higher education and research, and a platform for developing competent, creative, broad-minded, ethically and socially responsible leaders of tomorrow.  Located on a beautiful campus in the cradle of civilizations, Bilkent University, with its diverse educational programs, scholarly research endeavours, and artistic and cultural activities, aims to help individuals develop themselves as critical, analytical and independent thinkers, and life-long learners. Currently, there are about 13,000 students placed in 10 faculties. Bilkent offers a vibrant international community with more than 800 faculty members, one-fourth of this number coming from 37 countries. The university has a Symphony Orchestra which performs about 30 concerts every year, inviting internationally renowned artists. Bilkent University is an equal opportunity employer. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Benefits include rent-free furnished housing on campus, air-fare, paid annual leave, health center access on both campuses, state and private medical insurance -premiums paid by the university-, lunch-vouchers, and free access to on-campus facilities such as Bilkent's top-notch library, and sports including fitness rooms,  semi-Olympic indoor swimming pool, outdoor and indoor tennis courts, squash courts, basketball and volleyball courts. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/FA2023": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Department of Fine Arts",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Department of Fine Arts | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in Department of Fine Arts The Department of Fine Arts at Bilkent University, Ankara, invites applications at all levels (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) for permanent or visiting positions. Bilkent University is an English-medium institution, and instruction is in English. The Department of Fine Arts emphasizes both high-quality artistic practice and research. Faculty duties include teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels, research, supervision of student projects, graduate theses and other related tasks. The department will consider candidates with backgrounds and interests especially related to contemporary art. Description of Responsibilities and Duties: Teach Contemporary Art and Drawing courses within the Fine Arts Program in the Faculty of Art, Design, and Architecture Mentor and advise students Assist in the admissions process by interviewing students Continued professional activity Active participation in shared governance of the university community through service to the program, school, and institution Other duties as assigned by the Dean of FADA Required Qualifications: Candidates are required to have a Ph.D. degree In-depth knowledge and expertise in digital design and production processes, and drawing Prior teaching experience A strong exhibition record Demonstrated ability to work closely, and in collaboration, with a diverse student body, faculty, staff and other colleagues Demonstrated ability and willingness to contribute to curriculum planning in the Faculty of Arts, Design and Architecture Demonstrated a history of engagement with and broad interest in contemporary visual and performing arts Preferred Qualifications: Experience in the classroom and/or mentoring and supporting the development of early career artists Curatorial experience Experience with emerging and industry-standard technology Ability to teach related theoretical and practical design skills to Bilkent University students on the undergraduate and graduate level Bilkent University stands for diversity and equal opportunities. For this reason, we favor a working environment composed of heterogeneous teams and seek to promote the careers of individuals who are underrepresented in our respective professional areas. Bilkent University – the first private, nonprofit university in Turkey – was founded on October 20, 1984, with the fundamental aim of creating a center of excellence in higher education and research. It is home to a vibrant international community with 40 different countries. The University campus is located about 12 km (10 miles) west of the center of Ankara, it covers an area of more than 300 hectares. It is respectful of sustainability and offers all the facilities for a quality of life and challenging teaching and learning. Informal inquiries are welcome and should be addressed to Yasemin Gümüş Ağca (yasemin.agca@bilkent.edu.tr). Applications should include: Cover Letter CV with a list of publications and exhibitions a short artistic research statement (maximum 500 words) a teaching statement (maximum 500 words) Digital Portfolio or website of Professional work Digital Portfolio or website of Student work Contact information for 3 references The initial interview will be held online and letters of recommendation will be requested for short-listed candidate(s). Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and the review will continue until the position is filled. Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/HIST2023Classic": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Classical Ottoman History (1300-1700)",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Classical Ottoman History (1300-1700) | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in Classical Ottoman History (1300-1700) × Applications for this position has been closed. The Department of History at Bilkent University invites applications for a tenure-track position of open rank in the Ottoman History of Classical Period (1300-1700). The candidate should be prepared to offer an undergraduate lecture on pre-Modern Ottoman History, as well as upper-level undergraduate courses and graduate courses on the specialized aspects of this history. Preference will be given to those who can demonstrate excellence in research, publications and teaching. The Department of History particularly welcome applications from scholars who will enhance standing thematic and interdisciplinary strengths in the department. Qualifications: Candidates must have completed the Ph.D. by September 30, 2023. Benefits include membership in a comprehensive group health plan (with a small monthly premium), a free, fully-furnished on-campus apartment, and support for travel for international conferences and possibly research. Application Instructions: Application deadline is September 30, 2023. To apply submit a letter of application, CV, statement of research interest and goals, sample publication, graduate transcripts and contact information of three referees. Only electronic applications will be accepted. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/HIST2026Europa": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in the History of Modern Europe, post 1700",
      "description": "Faculty Position in the History of Modern Europe, post 1700 | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in the History of Modern Europe, post 1700 × Applications for this position has been closed. The Department of History at Bilkent University invites applications for a tenure-track position of open rank in Modern European History. The candidate should be able to offer graduate courses on their specialised aspects of the history of Europe after AD 1700, as well as undergraduate lectures on Modern European History and upper-level undergraduate courses. Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate excellence in research, publications, and teaching. The Department of History particularly welcomes applications from scholars who will enhance the department's existing thematic and interdisciplinary strengths. Qualifications: A doctorate degree in History is required. Benefits include membership of a comprehensive group health plan (with a small monthly premium), a free, fully furnished on-campus apartment, and support for travel to international conferences and research. For information about the History Department, please visit: https://history.bilkent.edu.tr/ For information about Bilkent University, please visit: https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent/ Application Instructions: The application deadline is 16 November 2025. Only electronic applications will be accepted. Online interviews of selected applicants will be held between 24-28 November 2025, and reference letters for these candidates will be requested at that time. Short-listed candidates will be invited for a campus visit in early-mid December 2025. For any enquiries, please contact Dr. David Thornton, chair of the Modern Europe Search Committee, at tdavid@bilkent.edu.tr Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/IE2022": {
      "title": "Multiple Faculty Positions in Department of Industrial Engineering",
      "description": "Multiple Faculty Positions in Department of Industrial Engineering | Applications for Faculty Positions Multiple Faculty Positions in Department of Industrial Engineering × Applications for this position has been closed. Department of Industrial Engineering at Bilkent University, Ankara, Turkey The Industrial Engineering Department at Bilkent University seeks candidates for multiple faculty positions beginning September, 2021. Appointments may be made at Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Full Professor positions. The candidate must have a PhD degree in a related field at the time of employment. The department emphasizes both high quality research and teaching. Faculty duties include research, teaching at graduate and undergraduate levels, supervision of master and Ph.D. students and other related tasks. Information about the department can be found at http://w3.ie.bilkent.edu.tr/ The department welcomes candidates with a strong fundamental background in one of the research fields: optimization, decision-making under uncertainty and risk, revenue management and pricing, production planning, simulation, statistics or data analytics. Candidates, who can build a strong methodological research base of operations research by contributing to application areas of high impact such as finance, health care, supply chain, sharing platforms or energy, are especially encouraged to apply. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. Faculty members are provided with research and teaching support, provision for international travel, comprehensive health coverage, pension and other benefits, and rent-free furnished housing on campus where the suburban location offers a pleasant living environment. For the first four years, new faculty members will have a reduced teaching load. There is also an excellent international school (with grades pre-K to 12) for faculty members with families. For more information on Bilkent University's programs and \nfacilities, visit https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent/ Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statements of teaching and research interests, sample publications or working papers, and the contact information of at least three references. There are also multiple Visiting Position opportunities for up to two years. If you are presenting at the 2022 INFORMS Annual Meeting, submitting at least a partial application package to Prof. Bahar Yetiş, Chair, E-mail: bkara@bilkent.edu.tr by October 5, 2022 with your session information would be helpful. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/IAED2021": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Department of Interior Architecture and Environmental Design",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Department of Interior Architecture and Environmental Design | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in Department of Interior Architecture and Environmental Design The Department of Interior Architecture and Environmental Design invites applications for appointment at all academic ranks (Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor). We seek to hire research-based positions. The medium of education at Bilkent University is English. The Faculty emphasizes cross-disciplinary approach to scholarship, design, and teaching. Faculty members are expected to engage in scholarly research, creative teaching, and service. Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in related fields (architecture, interior design/architecture) Strong research experience and publication record; publications in refereed/indexed international journals Strong portfolio (if applicable) Teaching experience Candidates are also expected to be able to teach design studio courses. The faculty at Bilkent University is comprised of an academic staff from around 40 different countries. Most of them were working in prominent universities in North America and Europe when they received offers from Bilkent University. According to ISI Citation Indexes, Bilkent ranks high in Turkey and internationally in number of published papers per faculty member. For more information about Bilkent University, please visit http://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent ; and Department of Interior Architecture and Environmental Design at iaed.bilkent.edu.tr . To apply, please provide the following documents: Cover letter Detailed CV Electronic copies of selected publications Names and contact information of three references Selected design projects or student work (if applicable) Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/IR2026": {
      "title": "Open Rank – Open Specialization in International Relations (Bilkent University)",
      "description": "Open Rank – Open Specialization in International Relations (Bilkent University) | Applications for Faculty Positions Open Rank – Open Specialization in International Relations (Bilkent University) × Applications for this position has been closed. Open Rank – Open Specialization in International Relations (Bilkent University). Assistant Professor in International Relations (Bilkent University). The Department of International Relations at Bilkent University invites applications for an open-rank (Asst/Assoc/Full Professor) position in international relations, to begin in September 2026. The department welcomes applications from scholars working in any area of specialization within the field of international relations broadly defined*. Candidates who can broaden our research and teaching portfolio and employ rigorous analytical and evidence-based methods (quantitative or qualitative) are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to produce world-class scholarly output evidenced by publications in leading peer-reviewed journals, and to contribute to the undergraduate and graduate programs in the department. The normal teaching load is 2+2, after an initial course reduction for early career researchers. Bilkent University offers a stimulating scholarly environment and a competitive compensation package, including free on-campus housing. Bilkent is an English-medium private university that provides stellar International Baccalaureate schooling options for school age children of faculty and a variety of campus facilities. To apply, candidates must submit: 1) CV, 2) cover letter that describes research and teaching interests, 3) contact information for three scholars who can provide letters of recommendation, to be requested if needed 4) a writing sample. Applicants are expected to have completed a Ph.D. in Political Science, International Relations or a related academic discipline by the beginning of the appointment. The deadline for submission is December 15, 2025. Bilkent University is an equal opportunity employer. The Department of International Relations welcomes applications from scholars with diverse backgrounds. Bilkent is the country's first private, non-profit university, and global rankings regularly highlight its place as one of the leading universities in Turkey. The Department of International Relations, which serves approximately 550 undergraduate students and 50 graduate students, fully embraces the university's foundational objectives of providing high-quality education, producing high-impact research, and serving the public in general. Please direct questions about the application process and the positions to ir@bilkent.edu.tr . To apply: https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/IR2026 * The department also conducts a separate open rank position search for scholars “whose research connects historical analysis to broader debates in international relations.” If you are interested in this position, please check the following link for the other ad: https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/IR2026H Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/IR2026H": {
      "title": "Open Rank Position in International Relations (Historical Approaches)",
      "description": "Open Rank Position in International Relations (Historical Approaches) | Applications for Faculty Positions Open Rank Position in International Relations (Historical Approaches) × Applications for this position has been closed. Open Rank Position in International Relations (Historical Approaches) The Department of International Relations at Bilkent University invites applications for an open rank (Asst/Assoc/Full Professor) position to begin in September 2026. We seek scholars whose research connects historical analysis to broader debates in international relations. Candidates working in Historical International Relations, Historical Political Economy, and Comparative Historical Analysis, who employ rigorous analytical and evidence-based methods (quantitative or qualitative) are encouraged to apply. We particularly welcome candidates with regional expertise who do research and can offer courses in their area of specialization.* The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to produce world-class scholarly output evidenced by publications in leading peer-reviewed journals, and to contribute to the undergraduate and graduate programs in the department, including teaching the department’s compulsory historical survey courses “Diplomatic History” and “20th Century World Politics”. The normal teaching load is 2+2, after an initial course reduction for early career researchers. Bilkent University offers a stimulating scholarly environment and a competitive compensation package, including free on-campus housing. Bilkent is an English-medium private university that provides stellar International Baccalaureate schooling options for school age children of faculty and a variety of campus facilities. To apply, candidates must submit: 1) CV, 2) cover letter that describes research and teaching interests, 3) contact information for three scholars who can provide letters of recommendation, to be requested if needed 4) a writing sample. Applicants are expected to have completed a Ph.D. in Political Science, International Relations or a related academic discipline by the beginning of the appointment. The deadline for submission is December 15, 2025. Bilkent University is an equal opportunity employer. The Department of International Relations welcomes applications from scholars with diverse backgrounds. Bilkent is the country's first private, non-profit university, and global rankings regularly highlight its place as one of the leading universities in Turkey. The Department of International Relations, which serves approximately 550 undergraduate students and 50 graduate students, fully embraces the university's foundational objectives of providing high-quality education, producing high-impact research, and serving the public in general. Please direct questions about the application process and the positions to ir@bilkent.edu.tr . *The department is also conducting a separate open rank & open specialization position search in international relations. If you are interested in that position, please check the following link for the other ad: https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/IR2026 Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/IF2024": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Faculty of Business Administration",
      "description": "Faculty Positions in Faculty of Business Administration | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Positions in Faculty of Business Administration Faculty Positions in Finance The Faculty of Business Administration at Bilkent University invites applications at all levels for a permanent or visiting position in the field of Finance. All research areas within Finance will be considered. Bilkent University is a private, nonprofit, research-intensive university located in Ankara, Turkey with an excellent research and teaching infrastructure. The Faculty of Business Administration is the first AACSB-accredited business school in Turkey offering BS, MBA, EMBA, MS and PhD degrees. The language of instruction is English. Successful candidates will be expected to conduct impactful research, teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, supervise graduate students, and take active part in the on-going academic development activities. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and the position to be applied for. Faculty members are provided with support for research and teaching, provision for international travel, comprehensive health coverage, pension and other benefits, and rent-free furnished housing on campus, where the suburban location offers a pleasant living environment. There is also an excellent international school (with grades pre-K to 12) for faculty members with families. For more information on Bilkent's programs and facilities, visit www.bilkent.edu.tr . Faculty Positions in Marketing The Faculty of Business Administration at Bilkent University invites applications at all levels for a permanent or visiting position in the field of Marketing. Bilkent University is a private, nonprofit, research-intensive university located in Ankara, Turkey with an excellent research and teaching infrastructure. The Faculty of Business Administration is the first AACSB-accredited business school in Turkey offering BS, MBA, EMBA, MS and PhD degrees. The language of instruction is English. Successful candidates will be expected to conduct impactful research, teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, supervise graduate students, and take active part in the on-going academic development activities.  Preference will be given to candidates with an interest in strategic marketing, branding, distribution channels, modeling, marketing research, or experimental consumer behavior. Individuals with backgrounds and/or research interests in the interface of marketing  with decision science and data analytics are also encouraged to apply. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. Faculty members are provided with support for research and teaching, provision for international travel, comprehensive health coverage, pension and other benefits, and rent-free furnished housing on campus, where the suburban location offers a pleasant living environment. There is also an excellent international school (with grades pre-K to 12) for faculty members with families. For more information on Bilkent's programs and facilities, visit www.bilkent.edu.tr . Faculty Positions in Accounting The Faculty of Business Administration at Bilkent University invites applications at all levels for a permanent or visiting position in the field of Accounting. Bilkent University is a private, nonprofit, research-intensive university located in Ankara, Turkey with an excellent research and teaching infrastructure. The Faculty of Business Administration is the first AACSB-accredited business school in Turkey offering BS, MBA, EMBA, MS and PhD degrees. The language of instruction is English. Successful candidates will be expected to conduct impactful research, teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, supervise graduate students, and take active part in the on-going academic development activities.  Applicants with interest in all areas in accounting are encouraged to apply. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. Faculty members are provided support for research and teaching, provision for international travel, comprehensive health coverage, pension and other benefits, and rent-free furnished housing on campus, where the suburban location offers a pleasant living environment. There is also an excellent international school (with grades pre-K to 12) for faculty members with families. For more information on Bilkent’s programs and facilities, visit www.bilkent.edu.tr . Faculty Positions in Operations Management The Faculty of Business Administration at Bilkent University invites applications at all levels for a permanent or visiting \nposition in the field of Operations Management. Bilkent University is a private, nonprofit, research-intensive university \nlocated in Ankara, Turkey with an excellent research and teaching infrastructure. The Faculty of Business Administration \nis the first AACSB-accredited business school in Turkey offering BS, MBA, EMBA, MS and PhD degrees. The language of \ninstruction is English. Successful candidates will be expected to conduct impactful research, teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, \nsupervise graduate students, and take active part in the on-going academic development activities. Preference will be given \nto candidates with an interest in operations management, operations strategy, or management science. Individuals with backgrounds \nand/or research interests in the interface of operations management with decision science, finance, marketing, accounting and data \nanalytics are also encouraged to apply. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. Faculty members are provided with support for research \nand teaching, provision for international travel, comprehensive health coverage, pension and other benefits, and rent-free \nfurnished housing on campus, where the suburban location offers a pleasant living environment. There is also an excellent \ninternational school (with grades pre-K to 12) for faculty members with families. For more information on Bilkent's \nprograms and facilities, visit www.bilkent.edu.tr Faculty Positions in Management The Faculty of Business Administration at Bilkent University invites applications for permanent and visiting positions \nin Management at any rank. Candidates in all subfields of management such as Organizational Behavior, Organizational Theory, \nStrategic Management and Entrepreneurship are invited to apply.  The Faculty of Business Administration is the first \nAACSB-accredited business school in Turkey offering BS, MBA, EMBA, MS and PhD degrees. The language of instruction is \nEnglish. Faculty of Business Administration ranks as the leader among the Turkish universities in all business related \nareas with respect to number of publications in a comparative study of Turkish universities between 2004 and 2014 \nannounced by the Scientific and Research Council of Turkey.For more information on Faculty of Business Administration, \nvisit www.man.bilkent.edu.tr . Successful candidates will be expected to conduct impactful research, teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, \nsupervise graduate students, and take active part in the on-going academic development activities. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. Faculty members are provided with research and teaching \nsupportive environment, provision for international travel, comprehensive health coverage, pension and other benefits, \nand rent-free furnished housing on campus, where the suburban location offers a pleasant living environment.  There is \nalso an excellent international school (with grades pre-K to 12) for faculty members with families.  For more information \non Bilkent's programs and facilities, visit www.bilkent.edu.tr . Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/ME2016": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Department of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Department of Mechanical Engineering | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in Department of Mechanical Engineering The Mechanical Engineering Department at Bilkent University invites applications for multiple tenure-track positions. Appointments may be made at Assistant Professor rank, as well as at Associate Professor or Full Professor rank for candidates with commensurate experiences and accomplishments. We will consider candidates in all areas of Mechanical Engineering. Applications in the areas of Manufacturing and Thermofluids are particularly encouraged. We seek exceptional candidates that can establish a vibrant, productive and well-funded research program with high international visibility. Commitment to excellence in teaching at undergraduate and graduate levels is a leading priority at Bilkent University. We expect all faculty members to contribute to the growth efforts of the department by taking service initiative in advancing its goals. Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/MBG2017": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics",
      "description": "Faculty Positions in Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Positions in Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics Bilkent University (Ankara, Turkey) invites qualified academics to apply for positions at the level of Instructor or Assistant or Associate Professor in the field of Molecular Biology and Genetics, and in particular, Genetics/Epigenetics, Genomics and Bioinformatics, Developmental and Cell Biology, Stem Cell Research, Gene Regulation, Infectious diseases and immunology, and Signal Transduction. The candidates are expected to undertake high quality, internationally leading research programs in line with the vision of the Department by obtaining extramural research funding and supervising research staff. The candidates are also expected to conduct teaching and educational activities at undergraduate and graduate levels, including supervision of graduate students. The University offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience along with a comprehensive fringe benefits package and on-campus housing. The Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics has been established in 1995 with the mission to make a strong contribution to Biological and Biomedical Sciences. Since then, many talented scientists from around the world and Turkey have joined the department as Scientific Leaders, Researchers, PhD and Master students, working in the fields of Cancer Biology, Genetics, Immunology, Genomics and Bioinformatics, Molecular and Cell Biology, and Genetics of Neurodegenerative Diseases and Complex Diseases. The department has extensive research collaborations with national and international research institutes, universities and hospitals, sharing the common goal to advance basic knowledge and translational research in Biological and Biomedical Sciences. For further information about the department, please visit: http://www.fen.bilkent.edu.tr/~bilmbg/ . Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/MUS2025V": {
      "title": "Faculty position in Voice for Department of Music in the Faculty of Music and Performing Arts",
      "description": "Faculty position in Voice for Department of Music in the Faculty of Music and Performing Arts | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty position in Voice for Department of Music in the Faculty of Music and Performing Arts Bilkent University Department of Music in the Faculty of Music and Performing Arts invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Voice, effective September 2025. The successful candidate will be expected to primarily teach applied voice lessons to majors and minors. A strong emphasis on voice pedagogy is desired. Additional teaching responsibilities may include coursework in the candidate's areas of expertise, such as voice literature, musical theater, choir, and other related subjects. Responsibilities include: Teach a studio of university-level voice students. Teach classroom courses related to voice, including voice pedagogy. Supervise student recitals Service on jury exams and committees as assigned. Recruit and retain talented voice students Other administrative duties as assigned Education Requirement: Doctorate in music (ABD is acceptable). Required Qualifications: Documented college-level experience in both studio voice and classroom instruction. Evidence of excellence in vocal performance artistry. Demonstrated expertise in voice pedagogy, with a strong foundation in healthy vocal technique across a range of styles. Bilkent University, located in suburban Ankara, is a non-profit foundation university supported by its own endowment. It is home to a vibrant international community. Its faculty members come from 40 different countries, and the language of instruction across the university is English. The university offers a competitive salary and a generous benefits package, including on-campus housing, health insurance, and subsidized private school for faculty members’ dependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. Applicants must upload a (i) cover letter, (ii) CV, and (iii) teaching statement. In addition, candidates are required to provide contact details for at least three referees. Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on May 15th and continue until the position is filled. Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/THEA2019M": {
      "title": "The Department of Performing Arts-Theatre at Bilkent University Faculty \nof Music and Performing Arts, Ankara, invites applications for an \nopen-rank full time faculty position/ Movement and Physical Theatre",
      "description": "The Department of Performing Arts-Theatre at Bilkent University Faculty \nof Music and Performing Arts, Ankara, invites applications for an \nopen-rank full time faculty position/ Movement and Physical Theatre | Applications for Faculty Positions The Department of Performing Arts-Theatre at Bilkent University Faculty \nof Music and Performing Arts, Ankara, invites applications for an \nopen-rank full time faculty position/ Movement and Physical Theatre × Applications for this position has been closed. Bilkent University seeks a professional artist/educator with expertise in Physical Theater and Movement to \nteach a range of undergraduate courses. Candidates with specialization in Suzuki method, Grotowski, \nBiomechanics or other similar methods and with the ability to also teach fundamentals of either \nFeldenkrais method, Alexander technique, Tai Chi or others are preferred. Primary responsibilities \ninclude design and teach a four-semester physical training curriculum for the undergraduate BA acting \nprogram. Other responsibilities include directing a physical theatre project, coaching/assisting department \nproductions, mentoring and advising students and participating in departmental and university service \nresponsibilities. Bilkent University, located in Ankara, is Turkey’s first private university.  The Department of Theatre, \nChaired by American Director Jason Hale, educates and trains undergraduate students to become actors and \ntheater artists, and enjoys a reputation of being a national first-choice for many students in Turkey. \nThe department provides the creative tools to become fully-equipped actors to our students and offer a \nrigorous curriculum with internationally-acclaimed, award-winning faculty and top-notch production \nfacilities and stages. Students are able to interpret, analyze and perform in a variety of disciplines \nand styles from classical plays to cutting-edge post-modern theatre, and from the stage to the screen. \nThe Department currently has international collaboration agreements with The Shanghai Theatre Academy \nand The Aleksander Zelwerowicz State Theatre Academy in Warsaw, Poland and is a member of ITI/UNESCO \nNetwork for Higher Education in the Performing Arts. Bilkent is a vibrant international community. Its faculty members come from 40 different countries, \nand the language of instruction across the university is English. MFA or MA in related field required. *All applications regardless of degree requirements will be considered. University level teaching experience, professional theatre experience, and a well-articulated \napproach to teaching movement for actors. Expertise in Physical Theatre. Candidates with additional specialization in related areas such as mask-work, stage combat, \ncommedia dell'arte, acrobatic skills, etc. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. Bilkent University provides fully furnished on \ncampus faculty housing, health insurance, lunch per diem, and subsidized private school for faculty members'\ndependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/THEA2024VS": {
      "title": "Open-rank full time faculty position/ Voice and Speech",
      "description": "Open-rank full time faculty position/ Voice and Speech at the Department of Performing Arts | Applications for Faculty Positions Open-rank full time faculty position/ Voice and Speech at the Department of Performing Arts Bilkent University's Department of Performing Arts seeks a professional artist/educator with expertise in voice training to teach a range of undergraduate courses. Responsibilities include: Candidates with certification in Linklater or Fitzmaurice Voicework are preferred. Primary responsibilities include designing and teaching a five-semester Voice training curriculum for the undergraduate BA acting program. Other responsibilities include coaching/assisting department productions, mentoring and advising students, and participating in departmental and university service responsibilities. Education Requirement: MFA or MA in related field required. *All applications, regardless of degree requirements, will be considered. Required Qualifications: University-level teaching experience, professional theatre experience, and a well-articulated approach to teaching Voice for actors Preferred Qualifications: Candidates specializing in related areas such as Shakespeare and classical acting. Salary and Benefits: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. Bilkent University provides fully furnished on-campus faculty housing, health insurance, lunch per diem, and subsidized private school for faculty members’ dependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. About Bilkent University: Bilkent University, located in Ankara, is Turkey’s first private university. The Department of Theatre, Chaired by American Director Jason Hale, educates and trains undergraduate students to become actors and theater artists, and enjoys a reputation of being a national first-choice for many students in Turkey. The department provides the creative tools to become fully-equipped actors to our students and offer a rigorous curriculum with internationally-acclaimed, award-winning faculty and top-notch production facilities and stages. Students are able to interpret, analyze and perform in a variety of disciplines and styles from classical plays to cutting-edge post-modern theatre, and from the stage to the screen. The Department currently has international collaboration agreements with The Shanghai Theatre Academy and The Aleksander Zelwerowicz State Theatre Academy in Warsaw, Poland and is a member of ITI/UNESCO Network for Higher Education in the Performing Arts. Bilkent is a vibrant international community. Its faculty members come from 40 different countries, and the language of instruction across the university is English. Applicants must upload a (i) Cirruculum Vitae, and (ii) letter of interest, and (iii) description of teaching and artistic philosophy. Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/PHYS2024": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Department of Physics",
      "description": "Faculty Positions in Department of Physics | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Positions in Department of Physics × Applications for this position has been closed. The Department of Physics at Bilkent University seeks candidates for permanent and visiting faculty positions at all levels starting in February and September 2024. We seek researchers with a Ph.D. in physics or related fields, working on Experimental Condensed Matter/Atomic Molecular and Optical Physics. Other applicants will not be considered. Successful candidates will be expected to conduct a vigorous research program and attract external funding. Considerable central resources are available at Bilkent that can strengthen the research program and support interdisciplinary and collaborative research efforts. Applications will be reviewed as they are received on an ongoing basis, and the search will continue until the positions are filled. Please contact the search committee chair at oktel@fen.bilkent.edu.tr for further information. Applications consisting of a cover letter, a resume, a statement of teaching philosophy, a brief (3-page limit) statement of research interests, and the names and addresses of two to four references should be submitted electronically. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/POLS2027T": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Department of Political Science and Public Administration (Turkish Politics)",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Department of Political Science and Public Administration (Turkish Politics) | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in Department of Political Science and Public Administration (Turkish Politics) The Department of Political Science and Public Administration at Bilkent University in Ankara, Turkey, invites applications for an open rank (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) position in T urkish Politics . Candidates must demonstrate an active research agenda and depending on seniority, a strong record of publication. They are also expected to offer high-quality teaching and training at undergraduate and graduate levels, particularly on Turkish Political Development and Contemporary Turkish Politics. The starting date is planned to be Spring or Fall of 2027. Applicants are expected to have a Ph.D. at the time of appointment. Regular teaching load is two courses per semester. Junior scholars may be eligible for reduced teaching load in their early semesters in the department. Bilkent University was founded in 1984. It has since been a leading research institution in Turkey. The medium of instruction is English. The University is an internationally diverse community with students and faculty.  Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. The university offers a generous benefit package including on-campus housing, health and retirement benefits as well as subsidized private school for faculty members' dependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. For further information about Bilkent University, please visit: http://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent/about-bilkent/ . How to apply: Please submit your application by uploading the following items at this address: https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/POLS2027T Cover letter Teaching statement Research statement CV Names and contact details of three referees (please have referees send their letters to pols@bilkent.edu.tr by the deadline). Two sample publications (e.g. articles, chapter of a monograph, dissertation chapters in case of continuing Ph.D. students.) Application deadline: 30 September 2026. Contact details: pols@bilkent.edu.tr Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/POLS2027P": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Department of Political Science and Public Administration (Political Theory)",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Department of Political Science and Public Administration (Political Theory) | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in Department of Political Science and Public Administration (Political Theory) The Department of Political Science and Public Administration at Bilkent University in Ankara, Turkey, invites applications for an open rank (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) position in Political Theory , with specialization in contemporary political theory . Candidates must demonstrate an active research agenda and depending on seniority, a strong record of publication.  They are also expected to offer high-quality teaching and training in political theory and introductory level political science at undergraduate and graduate levels. The starting date is planned to be Spring or Fall of 2027. Applicants are expected to have a Ph.D. at the time of appointment. Regular teaching load is two courses per semester. Junior scholars may be eligible for reduced teaching load in their early semesters in the department. Bilkent University was founded in 1984. It has since been a leading research institution in Turkey. The medium of instruction is English. The University is an internationally diverse community with students and faculty.  Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications. The university offers a generous benefit package including on-campus housing, health and retirement benefits as well as subsidized private school for faculty members' dependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. For further information about Bilkent University, please visit: http://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent/about-bilkent/ . How to apply: Please submit your application by uploading the following items at this address: https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/POLS2027P Cover letter Teaching statement Research statement CV Names and contact details of three referees (please have referees send their letters to pols@bilkent.edu.tr by the deadline). Two sample publications (e.g. articles, chapter of a monograph, dissertation chapters in case of continuing Ph.D. students.) Application deadline: 30 September 2026. Contact details: pols@bilkent.edu.tr Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/PSYC2026OR": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Positions",
      "description": "Open-Rank Positions at the Department of Psychology, Bilkent University | Applications for Faculty Positions Open-Rank Positions at the Department of Psychology, Bilkent University × Applications for this position has been closed. Bilkent University invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions (rank open) in the Department of Psychology. In line with the university’s strategic plan to expand the department ( psy.bilkent.edu.tr ), we welcome applications for multiple positions from promising and established scholars across all areas of psychology. Outstanding applicants from all subfields (social, developmental, cognitive, clinical) are strongly encouraged to apply. Qualifications and Responsibilities: Applicants should have a Ph.D. in psychology or a related discipline, and should have an excellent publication record (requirements vary with rank). A demonstrated ability or the potential to secure external research funding will be a strong advantage. Faculty members are expected to maintain productive research programs. Successful applicants will teach 2 courses per semester (with no teaching requirement during summers, and a possibility of reduced teaching in the first year of appointment), and supervise Ph.D., and Master’s students. Appointment: The full-time appointment will begin in September 2026 (negotiable). Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. The language of instruction at Bilkent is English. The Psychology Department serves around 400 undergraduate students, 50 graduate students, and strives for excellence in teaching and world-class research. Both the Psychology Department and the Interdisciplinary Graduate Program in Neuroscience (neuro.bilkent.edu.tr), where a number of faculty are jointly affiliated, offer Master’s and Ph.D. programs. For 5 consecutive years, each newly admitted Psychology major has scored in the top 6% or higher on the national university entrance exam. The Department has newly renovated research laboratories, as well as access to the university’s state-of-the-art facilities, which include a 3 Tesla MRI scanner, animal research center, and EEG equipment. Bilkent is located in Ankara, Turkey’s metropolitan capital, with daily direct flights to Istanbul and other major European cities. Bilkent University provides faculty members and their families with free housing, access to private health insurance, International Baccalaureate schooling options for dependents, and other benefits. Applicants should submit Cover letter CV Teaching Statement Research Statement PDF copies of 3 Representative Publications Contact Information for 3 Professional References The review of applications will begin immediately on a rolling basis and will continue until the positions are filled. The final deadline for full consideration is January 15, 2026. Applications can be submitted through the application portal ( https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/PSYC2026OR ). For more information regarding the Psychology Department and Bilkent University, please visit the following websites: psy.bilkent.edu.tr neuro.bilkent.edu.tr feass.bilkent.edu.tr bilkent.edu.tr Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/PSYC2026SP": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Faculty Positions in Social Psychology",
      "description": "Open-Rank Faculty Positions in Social Psychology at the Department of Psychology, Bilkent University | Applications for Faculty Positions Open-Rank Faculty Positions in Social Psychology at the Department of Psychology, Bilkent University × Applications for this position has been closed. In line with its goal of targeted expansion, the Department of Psychology at Bilkent University invites applications for tenure-track or tenured faculty positions (all ranks) in Social Psychology. Multiple positions may be available. The Department of Psychology has a strong focus on experimental psychology across its research and teaching programs and maintains close affiliations with the Neuroscience Graduate Program. We welcome applications from social psychologists or social neuroscientists working in any area of social psychology, including—but not limited to—personality, social cognition, perception, judgment, intergroup or interpersonal relations, and health psychology. Qualifications and Responsibilities Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in Social Psychology or a closely related field and have an excellent record of research and publication (expectations vary by rank). Demonstrated success or strong potential in securing external research funding will be considered an asset. Faculty members are expected to maintain a productive research program, teach two courses per semester (with no teaching requirements during the summer and possible reduced teaching in the first year), and contribute to undergraduate and graduate education in Social Psychology and statistics. They will also supervise Master’s and Ph.D. students. Appointment: The full-time appointment will begin in September 2026 (negotiable). Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. The language of instruction at Bilkent is English. The Psychology Department serves around 400 undergraduate students, 50 graduate students, and strives for excellence in teaching and world-class research. Both the Psychology Department and the Interdisciplinary Program in Neuroscience offer Master’s and Ph.D. programs. For 5 consecutive years, each newly admitted Psychology major has scored in the top 6% or higher on the national university entrance exam. The Department has newly renovated research laboratories, as well as access to the university’s state-of-the-art facilities, which include a 3 Tesla MRI scanner, animal research center, and EEG equipment. Bilkent is located in Ankara, Turkey’s metropolitan capital, with daily direct flights to Istanbul and other major European cities. Bilkent University provides faculty members and their families with free housing, access to private health insurance, International Baccalaureate schooling options for dependents, and other benefits. Applicants should submit Cover letter CV Teaching Statement Research Statement PDF copies of 3 Representative Publications Contact Information for 3 Professional References The review of applications will begin immediately on a rolling basis and will continue until the positions are filled. The final deadline for full consideration is January 15, 2026. Applications can be submitted through the application portal ( https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/PSYC2026SP ). For more information regarding the Psychology Department and Bilkent University, please visit the following websites: psy.bilkent.edu.tr neuro.bilkent.edu.tr feass.bilkent.edu.tr bilkent.edu.tr Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/THM2022": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Department of Tourism and Hotel Management",
      "description": "Faculty Positions in Department of Tourism and Hotel Management | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Positions in Department of Tourism and Hotel Management × Applications for this position has been closed. Bilkent University, Department of Tourism and Hotel Management The Department of Tourism and Hotel Management at Bilkent University is hiring additional faculty members. Applications are invited for the following full-time positions: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor in Tourism/Hospitality. The department emphasizes both high-quality research and teaching. Faculty duties include teaching at the undergraduate level, research, and senior project supervision. Applicants are expected to have a Ph.D. in Tourism, Hospitality, or a related field at the time of appointment. Candidates demonstrating an active and methodologically rigorous research agenda and a strong record of publications along with a record of high-quality teaching in an English medium university will be preferred. Bilkent University is an equal opportunity employer. At Bilkent, we emphasize interdisciplinary research, university-industry collaboration, and innovative teaching. The university offers internationally competitive salaries and benefits packages, including furnished housing. Each application should describe the professional interests and goals of the candidate in both teaching and research; include a resume with courses taught and a proof of proficiency in English (KPDS, IELTS or TOEFL exam scores) and the names and contact information of three or more individuals who will provide letters of recommendation. Application deadline: January 10, 2022 Further information on Bilkent University, Department of Tourism and Hotel Management is available at the following site: http://thm.bilkent.edu.tr/ . All questions regarding the available positions can be forwarded to the department chair: Asst. Prof. Eda Gürel Chair Department of Tourism and Hotel Management Bilkent University 06800 Ankara Turkey Email: eda@tourism.bilkent.edu.tr Phone: + 90 312 290 50 26 Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/TRIN2025": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor/ Professor position in Department of Translation and Interpretation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor/ Professor position in Department of Translation and Interpretation | Applications for Faculty Positions Assistant Professor/ Associate Professor/ Professor position in Department of Translation and Interpretation × Applications for this position has been closed. One position (rank: open) commencing September 2025. The Department of Translation and Interpretation at Bilkent University invites applications for one full-time open rank position for English and/or French courses. Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in Translation Studies, or related subjects at the time of appointment. Native or near-native fluency in English, and/or French, and/or Turkish is required. All candidates should have an active research agenda. The Translation and Interpretation Department at Bilkent University offers a dynamic and highly respected undergraduate program that prepares students for careers in the translation and interpreting fields. The department is home to a diverse faculty of experienced academics who are committed to helping students develop the skills and knowledge necessary to succeed in the field for the last 30 years. Students have the opportunity to learn from experts in a wide range of specialties, including translation theory; translation in special fields, including audio-visual translation and localization; and interpreting in different settings. Recognized as a center of excellence by the European Union institutions, the Department also offers a non-thesis graduate program in conference interpreting following the AIIC and the EMCI criteria for teaching conference interpreting. Bilkent University, located in suburban Ankara, is a non-profit foundation university supported by its own endowment. It is home to a vibrant international community. Its faculty members come from 40 different countries. The university offers a generous benefits package, including on-campus housing, health insurance, and subsidized private school for faculty members' dependents in the K-12 levels leading to an IB degree. As research is a priority at Bilkent University, its support includes grants for conference travel and the possibility of a sabbatical leave after the third year. Should you have any queries regarding the position, please email the search committee at trinjobs@bilkent.edu.tr . Applicants must upload a (i) cover letter (ii) CV (iii) research statement (iv) teaching statement, and (v) writing sample. In addition, (vi) candidates are required to provide contact details for at least three referees. Deadline for applications: January 15, 2025. VERSION FRANÇAISE : Le département de traduction et d'interprétation de l'Université Bilkent a le plaisir d'annoncer l'ouverture d'un poste de professeur à plein temps. Les candidats doivent être titulaires d'un doctorat en traductologie ou dans un domaine connexe au moment de la nomination. La maîtrise de l'anglais, du français ou du turc est requise. Tou.te.s les candidat.e.s doivent avoir un plan de recherche bien défini. La recherche étant une priorité à l'université Bilkent, celle-ci offre un soutien sous forme de subventions pour les voyages de conférence ainsi que la possibilité de bénéficier d'un congé sabbatique après trois années d'emploi. Pour toute question relative au poste, veuillez contacter le comité de recherche par courriel à l'adresse trinjobs@bilkent.edu.tr Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/EDEB2016": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Turkish Literature (Modern Turkish Lit.)",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Turkish Literature (Modern Turkish Lit.) | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Position in Turkish Literature (Modern Turkish Lit.) × Applications for this position has been closed. The Department of Turkish Literature at Bilkent University invites applications for a faculty appointment (open rank) in Modern Turkish Literature, Comparative and World Literature. While the field of specialization is open, we are particularly interested in candidates with a demonstrated ability to teach graduate courses in comparative literary studies, literary theory and/or criticism that situate Modern Turkish Literature (from the Tanzimat Era to the present) within broader regional and global contexts, in addition to general courses in comparative literature, literary theory, and literary criticism. Preference will be given to those who can demonstrate excellence in research, publications and teaching. An ability to teach in Turkish is welcome but not required. Academic rank, salary and teaching-load will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Benefits include membership in a comprehensive group health plan (with a small monthly premium), a free, fully-furnished on-campus apartment, and support for travel for international conferences. Bilkent University, located in suburban Ankara, was founded in 1984 as the first private research university in Turkey. The medium of instruction throughout the university is English. The Department of Turkish Literature, established in 1998 focuses only on graduate education. More information about the university can be found at its website: bilkent.edu.tr Applicants should submit a letter of application; sample publications; a description of interests in research and teaching; relevant transcripts; a curriculum vitae; contact information for 3 professional references. Position will be open until it is filled. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/LAUD2026": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Department of Urban Design and Landscape Architecture (Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor)",
      "description": "Faculty Positions in Department of Urban Design and Landscape Architecture (Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor) | Applications for Faculty Positions Faculty Positions in Department of Urban Design and Landscape Architecture (Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor) The Department of Urban Design and Landscape Architecture (LAUD) at Bilkent University invites applications for full-time appointments at the rank of all levels (Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor). We seek to hire for research and practice-based positions. These positions are open until they are filled. Bilkent University is an equal opportunity employer with an international body of faculty and students. The medium of education is English. The faculty is comprised of academic staff from around 40 different countries. Most of them were working in prominent universities in North America and Europe when they received offers from Bilkent University. According to ISI Citation Indexes, Bilkent ranks high in Turkey and internationally in number of published papers per faculty member. Bilkent University ranks 28th in Times Higher Education’s 100 Under 50 list of the world’s best young universities. For more information about Bilkent University and LAUD, please visit https://w3.bilkent.edu.tr/bilkent/ and http://www.laud.bilkent.edu.tr/ Bilkent University, Department of Urban Design and Landscape Architecture is a design-oriented program that bridges Urban Design and Landscape Architecture. It fulfills a unique and leading role in undergraduate education of urban design in Turkey. LAUD's multi-disciplinary faculty and open, pluralistic attitude to education enrich its students with social, environmental and aesthetic values. With a multidisciplinary faculty and an innovative educational model, the department invites applications for full-time positions at all ranks in architecture and landscape architecture. Teaching capability that actively and creatively  addresses contemporary and emerging topics in landscape architecture, urban studies, and spatial design is a core value at LAUD. Faculty members are expected to engage in cross-disciplinary dialogue, creative teaching, scholarly research, and service to the department. QUALIFICATIONS FOR THE RESEARCH-BASED POSITION (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor): Undergraduate training in architecture, landscape architecture, urban planning or related fields. PhD degree in architecture, landscape architecture, urban design, urban planning, environmental design, or related fields in humanities, social sciences, or environmental sciences Publications in refereed/indexed international journals Teaching experience and capability to teach in one or more of the following areas: Urban studies Ecology / environmental design History and theory Basic design and/or urban design studio courses QUALIFICATIONS FOR THE PRACTICE-BASED POSITION (Instructor): Undergraduate and graduate training in architecture, landscape architecture or urban design. Teaching experience and capability to teach in one or more of the following areas: Construction, materials and site design Plant Material / botany Professional practice and design Basic design and/or urban design studio courses APPLICANTS SHOULD SUBMIT THE FOLLOWING MATERIALS: A cover letter describing qualifications for the position, as well as current and future research plans. A current curriculum vitae. A teaching statement. A research statement. (For research-based position) Electronic copies of selected publication. (For research-based position) A portfolio. (For practice-based position) Contact information (mail, email, phone) for three academic references. (Optional) Evidence of teaching excellence (e.g., teaching evaluations). Applicants will need to apply online using the university’s online application system. Submit New Application Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/FRL2024": {
      "title": "Instructor Positions in the Foreign Language Unit, Bilkent University",
      "description": "Instructor Positions in the Foreign Language Unit, Bilkent University | Applications for Faculty Positions Instructor Positions in the Foreign Language Unit, Bilkent University × Applications for this position has been closed. Three positions, commencing September 2024. The Foreign Language Unit at Bilkent University invites applications for up to three full-time Instructors to teach French, German, Spanish, or Turkish as a foreign language. At the time of application candidates must have: Diploma: At least a Master’s degree in Foreign Language Teaching (or related subjects). Teaching experience: At least one year in the target foreign language. Target foreign language proficiency: Level C1/C2 or YDS with a minimum of 85 points (scores valid for 5 years). ALES: At least 70 points for Equal Weighted or Verbal (scores valid for 5 years). PhD holders do not need to provide an ALES score. English language proficiency: At least B1/B2 (scores valid for 2 years). In addition, candidates are required to provide a CV and contact details for at least three referees. Successful applicants will be expected to teach a total of nine courses per year (with a typical class size of 15-20 students). Should you have any questions, please contact the search committee at fhl@bilkent.edu.tr . Note : We are only accepting applications via Bilkent University’s online application system . Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/CCI2024": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Full-time Tenure Track Position in Program in Cultures, Civilizations and Ideas",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Full-time Tenure Track Position in Program in Cultures, Civilizations and Ideas | Applications for Faculty Positions Assistant Professor, Full-time Tenure Track Position in Program in Cultures, Civilizations and Ideas × Applications for this position has been closed. Bilkent University’s Faculty of Humanities and Letters announces multiple openings in the Program in Cultures, Civilizations & Ideas. The CCI Program is staffed by an interdisciplinary team of scholars from diverse fields in the humanities and is primarily responsible for teaching a mandatory two-semester sequence of courses in literature and philosophy to most undergraduates at the University. Additional teaching opportunities, such as honors seminars and humanities electives, arise occasionally. Requirements: Candidates should have a PhD in a field in the humanities completed before September 2024. All applicants should have a publication record commensurate with their career stage and evidence of future research potential in their field. We welcome those with excellent records of teaching at the college level and who enjoy engaging with students from diverse backgrounds. In addition to specialized expertise in their own fields, candidates should demonstrate proficiency in teaching works of philosophy and literature from different eras and traditions, as well as a broad educational background in the humanities. Scholars committed to interdisciplinary and comparative work, whether in their research or their teaching, are particularly encouraged to apply. Experience in teaching text-based “Great Books” courses is especially desirable. Initial screening interviews will be held via Zoom beginning in January 2024. Duties: Expected starting date is September, 2024. Standard teaching load is 3-3 (one prep), with a teaching load reduction for new faculty members in the first three semesters. An active research agenda is expected. Support includes substantial funding for conference travel and potential for sabbatical leave following the third year. Our service load tends to be modest, but each department member is expected to contribute. Bilkent University, located in Ankara, is the oldest independent non-profit research university in Turkey. All classes are conducted in English.  Salary is competitive and includes a fully furnished and rent-free apartment on campus. Applications are to be made online at: https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/CCI2024 .  Complete applications must include a Curriculum Vitae, a letter of application specific to this position, a detailed 5-year research plan and a teaching statement to be submitted online.  For assistance, contact Dr. Mustafa Nakeeb, Coordinator, at mnakeeb@bilkent.edu.tr .  Application deadline is 15 December, 2023 19:00 UTC+3. Edit Existing Application"
    },
    "https://stars.bilkent.edu.tr/staffapp/NSC2026": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Position, Department of Neuroscience",
      "description": "Open-Rank Position, Department of Neuroscience at Bilkent University | Applications for Faculty Positions Open-Rank Position, Department of Neuroscience at Bilkent University × Applications for this position has been closed. Bilkent University invites applications for multiple open-rank faculty positions in the Department of Neuroscience. The department plans to expand research activities in certain focus areas and accordingly seeks applications from established or promising scholars who have worked in the following or related fields: Computational/theoretical neuroscience with a strong emphasis on research involving emerging approaches, including artificial intelligence, big-data analytics, neuronal modeling, brain-machine interfaces, and robotics. Systems/cognitive neuroscience with a strong emphasis on visual, auditory, somatosensory, motor, language, learning, and memory domains, or multi-domain investigations. Cellular/molecular neuroscience with a strong emphasis on research focusing on cognitive studies involving preclinical models or humans. The Department’s interdisciplinary Graduate Program in Neuroscience, which offers Master's and PhD degrees, was established in 2014. The department is affiliated with Bilkent’s Aysel Sabuncu Brain Research Center (ASBAM) and the National Magnetic Resonance Research Center (UMRAM). Faculty affiliated with the department have the privilege to access state-of-the-art research facilities in these centers, including animal facilities, cellular/molecular laboratory infrastructure, psychophysics laboratories, eye-tracking laboratories, EEG laboratories, a human-robot interaction laboratory, and two MRI scanners (3T and 1.5T). Bilkent is located in Ankara, Turkey's metropolitan capital, with daily direct flights to Istanbul and other major European cities. Bilkent University provides faculty members and their families with free housing, access to private health insurance, International Baccalaureate schooling options for dependents, and other benefits. Qualifications and Responsibilities Applicants should have a PhD in neuroscience or a related discipline and should have an excellent publication record (requirements vary with rank). A demonstrated ability or the potential to secure external research funding will be a strong advantage. Faculty members are expected to maintain productive research programs. Successful applicants will supervise PhD and Master's students and teach during the Fall and Spring semesters, with no teaching requirement during the summer. Appointment The full-time appointments can begin as soon as a successful applicant is identified, although the starting date is negotiable. Salary will be internationally competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Application Procedure Applicants should submit a cover letter; CV; research statement; teaching statement; pdf copies of 3 most important publications; and contact information for 3-5 professional references. Review of applications will start immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications can be submitted through the application portal. Inquiries can be directed to nsc-admin@bilkent.edu.tr or +90 312 290 3002. For more information, please visit the following websites: neuro.bilkent.edu.tr umram.bilkent.edu.tr beyin.bilkent.edu.tr bilkent.edu.tr Edit Existing Application"
    }
  },
